:sdx_ds_leds_plug:
> **On** (default): at every load the driver gets `leds_enabled=1` on each of the three 88SE9215 controllers (DSM's own three init values, `research/2026-10-25-bay-leds.md`): green then shows presence and activity. The first one also sets Avoton PCH GPIO 49 high, which DSM's synobios does before its first disk LED and which the orange LEDs need (`research/2026-10-26-ds-orange-led.md`). **Off**: `leds_enabled=0`, the controllers get back the values found at load and GPIO 49 its value at load; the bays stay dark and no orange can show.
:end

DX1215 bay LEDs (DX_LEDS):
: <select name="DX_LEDS" aria-label="DX1215 bay LEDs (DX_LEDS)">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['DX_LEDS'], "1", "On (default)")?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['DX_LEDS'], "0", "Off")?>
  </select>

:sdx_dx_leds_plug:
> **On** (default): `unit/dx_leds_enabled=1` clears the disk-LED mask (page 1 bit 6) on all four port multipliers; each write is one short libata error-handler round with readback. **Off**: sets the mask again (the power-on state measured on this unit). Orange on the DX1215 is a separate bit per bay (`hostN/fault`), shown only while the mask is clear.
:end

